ns1:GO_0008150 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "biological_process" ;
    ns1:IAO_0000115 "A biological process is the execution of a genetically-encoded biological module or program. It consists of all the steps required to achieve the specific biological objective of the module. A biological process is accomplished by a particular set of molecular functions carried out by specific gene products (or macromolecular complexes), often in a highly regulated manner and in a particular temporal sequence." .

